    <string name="charging_extreme_title">Enable Extreme Charging?</string>
    <string name="charging_extreme_message">Charges at the maximum the charger can supply. Only activates at or below 60%% battery, pauses when the battery reaches 43 °C, and turns itself off above 60%% or when unplugged.\n\nThe battery will get warm. Do not use a case that traps heat.</string>
    <string name="charging_limit_title_warning">Force Limit Charging</string>
    <string name="charging_limit_message">Holds charging at the wattage you select. Use a charger that can actually supply it — on a weaker charger the phone will fall short and you will be told.\n\nIf the device becomes too hot, this setting turns itself off automatically.</string>
    <string name="charging_high_message">You selected a high wattage. The phone will run warm and may throttle itself. If it gets too hot this setting turns off automatically.</string>

